---
import Breadcrumb from "../components/Breadcrumb.astro";
import { contactUrl } from "../config";
import { href } from "../lib/paths";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const description =
  "Ask about a sponsored listing on PrivateAsync. Listings would be labelled and kept separate from the alphabetical table. Pricing is not set. No payment on this site.";
---

<Base title="Get featured | PrivateAsync" description={description}>
  <Breadcrumb items={[{ name: "Home", href: href("/") }, { name: "Get featured" }]} />
  <h1>Get featured</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A featured listing would be a labelled “Sponsored” block, separate from the alphabetical table. Pricing is not set. There is no payment on this site, and there are no featured slots on the directory today.
  </p>
  <h2>What a listing would be</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Placed outside the ranked table, not mixed into alphabetical order.</li>
    <li>Labelled Sponsored, in the same plain way an affiliate link is labelled.</li>
    <li>Unable to change the verified facts. Price, encryption claim, open source, self-hosting, jurisdiction, and the verified date stay as checked.</li>
    <li>Able to include a logo and a short blurb supplied by the vendor. That blurb would be labelled as the vendor’s text, not as a checked fact.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>What this page is not</h2>
  <p>
    It is not a checkout, a rate card, or a promise that a listing is available. To ask about one, use the publisher’s Gumroad page. The answer can be no.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a class="button" href={contactUrl} rel="noopener" target="_blank">Contact via Gumroad</a>
  </p>
  <p>Affiliate links, which are different from a featured block, are described on the <a href={href("/affiliate-disclosure")}>affiliate disclosure</a> page.</p>
</Base>
